@page "/"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<h1>Circuit pause</h1>

<p>
    This component runs in an interactive Server circuit. Two ways to pause it:
</p>

<div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">
    <strong>Quick test:</strong>
    Increment the counter, then use the button below to pause every active circuit.
    The pause response opens in a new tab so this page remains available for testing.
    <a class="btn btn-warning btn-sm ms-2" href="/pause-all" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Pause all circuits
    </a>
</div>

<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Server-initiated pause:</strong>
        <code>Circuit.RequestCircuitPauseAsync()</code>. The button above calls
        <code>/pause-all</code> while this page is open. The server asks the
        client to begin the graceful circuit-pause flow (used to drain circuits
        during deployments).
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Automatic pause (opt-in):</strong> hide this tab for
        &gt; 30 seconds (<code>AddAutoPause</code> with
        <code>HiddenDelay</code>). The circuit pauses itself and releases
        server resources until you come back.
    </li>
</ul>

<div class="card" style="max-width: 320px">
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="card-text">
            If the circuit is paused, clicking the button re-activates it
            (state is preserved).
        </p>
        <p>
            Count: <strong>@_count</strong>
        </p>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="Increment">Increment</button>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    int _count;

    private void Increment() => _count++;
}
